<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yaroslav of Tver</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1230">1230</a>–<a href="/years/1271">1271</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Yaroslav III of Vladimir, Yaroslav Yaroslavich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yaroslav Yaroslavich was the first Prince of Tver, from about 1247, and Grand Prince of Vladimir from 1264 to 1271. A younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a>, he founded the dynasty that ruled Tver until 1485 and as grand prince clashed with Novgorod, which accepted him only under written conditions. He died returning from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> in 1271.</p></div>
